**Sub-beats:** SB-A grid/panel assembly (with timeline + figure as set) · SB-B strike sweep 1 (incl. ring lifecycle: day-16 plain ring converts to ⊗ as the sweep passes it, day-34 plain ring forms) · SB-C drop-line 2 · SB-D timeline labels (A struck, B lands) · SB-E hold · SB-F tasks panel joins + strike sweep 2 · SB-G strike sweep 3 + tasks rows complete · SB-H final strikes (incl. day 35's slash) + day-34 ⊗ conversion + label-B strike + arc fade · SB-I final hold.

### 1.4 Variables (§1.3 extraction)
1. Grid — columns, rows, first day numeral, numeral strings (derived from firstDay + index), cell geometry (derived from panel + cols/rows), numeral font size.
2. Marks — strike sweep targets per phase (counts), strike order (derived reading order), ring cells (early-ring index, cross-ring index, late-ring index), ring radius, strike stroke width.
3. Drop-lines — drop targets (cell indices, derived from ring cells: drop 1 from ringEarly's cell, drop 2 from ringLate's cell), dash pattern, timeline label texts (A/B), label strike treatment — ONE treatment for both labels, binding (jev-observe-exit charge 2): each label strike is an **X** (two diagonals over the label's ink box) drawn by that label's strikeP 0→1; label A's strikeP runs across the labels phase, label B's across the final phase; the treatment is identical at strike time and at the final hold (no form change between phases).
4. Tasks panel — title text, checkbox row counts (join count, total count), row line style, panel join travel.
5. Set — timeline Y + tick count, figure centre/scale, arc opacity arc (present → faded at final), panel shift distance when tasks joins.
6. Timing — grid duration, sweep-1 duration, drop-line duration, labels duration, hold-1, tasks-join duration, sweep-3 duration, final duration, final hold; phase starts DERIVED sequentially (never independent keys).
7. Palette — background, ink, faint ink (struck numerals dim), panel stroke, strike ink.
8. Text — panel titles (days/tasks), font family + sizes for titles, numerals, timeline labels.

### 1.5 Guidance dispositions (inline, A9.5)
- A1 §2 typography precedent: NOT APPLICABLE — no particle typography; numerals/labels are SVG text rendered from CONFIG.
- A5 Owner Cures 1–2: NOT APPLICABLE as particle cures — no particle field, no phrase lifecycle. The analogue carried: **phase exclusivity by construction** — phases are sequential-derived and the named draw-on order (grid → strikes → drop-lines → timeline labels) is enforced by the phase machine; a later phase's progress is 0 until its derived start (harness-asserted).
- A5 §4 flow-field model: NOT APPLICABLE — no particle pool.
- A9.1 plate construction: NOT APPLICABLE — no moving background plate; the background is still black. The tasks panel's join travel is a panel entrance, priced as geometry in §2.1, not a plate.
- Sibling cures carried binding (T233 Wave 37 + T232/T227 Wave 36 NO-VERDICT receipt-form cures, same fleet record): every census probe carries its CONFIG expression · each fixed census probe is paired with an EXECUTABLE CONFIG-derived companion assertion whose instant is computed (not a label string) and which MOVES under the timing swap · full predicates executed (not subsets) at labelled checkpoints · raw phase value and eased result printed separately where easing applies (this build is linear-progress by design — easings are CONFIG names applied to phase progress; raw == eased only when the CONFIG easing is "linear", printed both ways).

## §2 — PLAN

### 2.1 Parameter table (every variable → CONFIG key; specimen value = default)
Top-level: `stageW 480 · stageH 520 · cols 7 · rows 5 · firstDay 1 · readingDir "rtl" · panelW 215 · panelH 200 · panelY 55 · panelR 10 · calShiftPx 100 · tasksGapPx 17 · numeralFontPx 21 · titleFontPx 15 · labelFontPx 21 · fontFamily "Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif" · daysTitle "DAYS" · tasksTitle "TASKS" · timelineLabelA "THAT DATE" · timelineLabelB "THIS TIME" · ringEarlyIdx 15 · ringLateIdx 33 · ringRPx 13 · ringFormFraction 0.25 · ringLateFormFraction 0.20 · strikeStrokePx 2 · labelStrikeStrokePx 2 · dropDash "5 5" · timelineY 460 · timelineTicks 15 · figureCx 300 · figureScale 1 · tasksRowsJoin 3 · tasksRowsTotal 5 · tasksLineStyle "dashed" · tasksTravelRatio 0.4 · strikes1Target 20 · strikes2Target 26 · strikes3Target 32 · strikesFinalTarget 35 · gridDurMs 1200 · strikes1DurMs 2000 · dropDurMs 600 · labelsDurMs 600 · hold1DurMs 1000 · tasksDurMs 1000 · sweep3DurMs 2000 · finalDurMs 2000 · holdMs 2000 · easeGrid/easeStrikes/easeDrop/easeLabels/easeTasks/easeFinal "linear" · palette {bg #000000, ink #f4f4f4, faint #7d7d7d, panel #f4f4f4, strike #f4f4f4}`. **Restage note (builder cure before prewave, priced in build-record):** the first-draft stage (640×440, numeralFontPx 15, labelFontPx 13) puts numeral ink at ≈6 px on the 360 px stage — under guard-measured-fit's ~11 px floor by measurement, not by model. The stage was re-proportioned to the specimen's portrait frame (480×520) and the font keys raised (numerals 21 · labels 21 · titles 15) with label A's gloss shortened ("THAT DATE" for فلان تاریخ) so every subject text row measures at/above the floor in the fit leg; the geometry keys above are the cured values the build carries.
Derived (named, never stored): dayCount = cols×rows (=35; count assertion: source-count 35 = built-count 35, harness-printed) · day label of cell i = String(firstDay + i) · cellW = panelW/cols · cellH = panelH/rows · strike order = index order 0..dayCount−1 (RTL reading is a rendering direction; the sweep's index order is the priced allocation of the census's row-wise progression) · phase starts: gridStart=0 · strikes1Start=gridStart+gridDurMs (=1200) · dropStart=strikes1Start+strikes1DurMs (=3200) · labelsStart=dropStart+dropDurMs (=3800) · hold1End=labelsStart+labelsDurMs (=4400) · tasksStart=hold1End+hold1DurMs (=5400) · sweep3Start=tasksStart+tasksDurMs (=6400) · finalStart=sweep3Start+sweep3DurMs (=8400) · completeAtMs=finalStart+finalDurMs (=10400) · durationMs=completeAtMs+holdMs (=12400) · strikeFloat(t): 0 before strikes1Start; →strikes1Target across strikes1; →strikes2Target across tasks phase; →strikes3Target across sweep3; →strikesFinalTarget across final · cell i strikeP = clamp(strikeFloat − i, 0, 1) (ring cells' strikeP drives their ⊗ cross instead of a slash — a ring cell renders slash XOR cross, never both) · **ONE ring-cross authority (codex-plan-review cure): both ring crosses are their cell's strikeP** — ringEarly crossP = strikeP(ringEarlyIdx), ringLate crossP = strikeP(ringLateIdx); marked-cell counts (strikesFull) count cells by strikeP ≥ 1, ring cells included on the same term · ringEarly: plain ring forms across the last ringFormFraction (0.25) of grid phase · ringLate: plain ring forms across the last ringLateFormFraction (0.20) of strikes1 · drop1P = gridP (census: drop-line 1 is set at first calendar frame; it falls from ringEarly's cell — **drop 1 is pre-existing SET, outside the named order's scope**, see order-scope note below) · drop2P across drop phase (falls from ringLate's cell) · labelA: VISIBLE from gridP (timeline set, opacity = gridP); its strikeP + labelB opacity run across labels phase · labelB strikeP across final phase (both label strikes X-form per §1.4 (3), drawn from each label's strikeP) · arcOpacity = gridP × (1 − finalP) · tasksP across tasks phase (panel slides from x+tasksTravelPx with opacity; tasksTravelPx = panelW × tasksTravelRatio derived) · tasksRowsVisible = tasksRowsJoin during tasks phase, → tasksRowsTotal across sweep3; tasks row lines render tasksLineStyle ("dashed") once sweep3 begins, solid during the join (census CP8000 solid → CP10000 dashed — a phase-derived style, the key names the final treatment) · calShiftP = tasksP (calendar group translates −calShiftPx × tasksP) · cell x positions derive from readingDir ("rtl": index 0 at the panel's right edge; "ltr" mirrors) · **palette hierarchy by construction:** unstruck numerals render palette.ink, struck numerals palette.faint, marks (strikes/crosses/rings) palette.strike — the harness asserts the FAINT role (struck numerals, dimmer than the marks over them) stays distinct from both ink and strike under the palette swap (default ink == strike: the specimen is monochrome white; the separation the technique needs is struck-numeral vs mark, priced at the cure round before prewave). **Order scope (codex-plan-review cure):** the named draw-on order governs exactly: grid assembly → strikes sweep 1 → drop-line 2 → timeline-label events (A strike + B reveal). Drop-line 1, the timeline, label A's TEXT, the figure and the arc are pre-existing set arriving with the grid phase (the census's first calendar frame already carries them); sweeps 2–3 and the final phase intentionally run CONCURRENT with the tasks join and label B's strike (the census shows strikes continuing while the tasks panel joins) — concurrency there is census behaviour, not an order violation. Phase exclusivity is asserted where the order claims it: drop2P = 0 before dropStart · labelA strikeP = 0 and labelB opacity = 0 before labelsStart (harness P4/P5 pre-conditions). **Validation:** durations >0 finite; targets strictly increasing and ≤ dayCount (final target = dayCount: every cell marked in the final state, per the cured §1.1 (3)); ring indices distinct and < dayCount; **ringEarlyIdx < strikes1Target AND ringLateIdx ≥ strikes3Target AND ringLateIdx < strikesFinalTarget** (each conversion completes inside its designated sweep); tasksRowsJoin ≤ tasksRowsTotal; fractions in (0,1); **bounds (jev-plan-exit): cols/rows positive integers with cols ≤ 10 and rows ≤ 8 · two panels + gap fit the stage (2×panelW + tasksGapPx ≤ stageW) · panelY + panelH < timelineY · ringRPx < min(cellW, cellH)/2 + ringRPx margin priced (ring may exceed the cell — census rings overlap neighbours slightly; the bound is ringRPx ≤ cellW, asserted)**; a violating CONFIG is rejected by validateConfig, never rendered (harness validator receipts: ring-index-out-of-range rejected · panel-overflow rejected).

### 2.2 Construction choice
**DOM/SVG single-stage scene (chosen):** one SVG; background rect; calendar group (panel rect + title tab + per-cell numeral text + per-cell strike line + ring marks) translating with calShiftP; tasks group (panel + title + checkbox rows) joining at tasks phase; timeline group (line + ticks + two labels with strike crosses + figure + dashed arc); dashed drop-lines from ring cells to the timeline. All geometry from `stateAt(cfg,t)`, a pure function evaluable in node; `window.__T243` exposed.
**Figure + arc disposition (§8 size discipline, codex-plan-review item 5 — applied in part with reason):** the figure and arc are SET, carried at minimal geometry (figure: head circle + body/leg path + chest star, from figureCx/figureScale; arc: one dashed quadratic path whose opacity is state-derived) — they are present because both drop-lines land on the timeline the figure stands on and the arc's disappearance is a census state change (CP12000) the checkpoints assert; a DETAILED figure reconstruction (proportions, star-crack glyph) is deferred as a later attempt's ornament, and no checkpoint asserts figure detail beyond presence + arcOpacity.
Rejected: Canvas 2D — loses per-element ink measurement the A6 fit leg needs. CSS keyframes — phase state not evaluable as a pure function (A11 receipts impossible). Photographic/generated imagery — approaches the specimen; the technique is the draw-on order, carried by geometry.
**Named deferrals (lawful, priced):** (1) Window head (source 13–17 s, T242's bars) — outside this technique; the allocation discards it (departure table §2.3). (2) The figure's chest-star crack at 26 s — the next beat's glyph; the build holds the final state. (3) The tail transition (≥26.5 s: dimming panels, tiny population figures) — next scene, not built. (4) The "perhaps…" annotation at 23 s — caption-adjacent scene text, not technique; not built. (5) Persian numeral glyphs + Persian label texts — the build renders CONFIG Latin strings (numerals derived from firstDay, labels as CONFIG text); the technique is the order + marks, not the specimen's language — the swap test re-labels freely, which is the parameterization proof. (6) The source's calendar entrance is unobserved (inside the 15→17 s gap): the build's grid phase is an ALLOCATION expanding that entrance so the named order reads — priced in §2.5, departure-tabled in §2.3. (7) The figure's lateral drift in the source (it tracks the calendar's shift and recentres by the final state) is simplified to a FIXED figureCx — the drop-lines land on the timeline at CONFIG-derived x positions in both readings; the drift is staging, not technique.

### 2.3 Census-anchor mapping (A10.2) + A11 assertions
Window-start offset: **t=0 allocation** — build 0 ms = source 17.0 s (segment-relative 4000 ms); build instant = census seg-rel − 4000 for the lifecycle anchors, with the opening-expansion departure below.
**Departure table:** (a) census CP0/CP2000 (seg-rel 0/2000, T242 bars) have NO build counterpart (deferral 1). (b) Census CP4000 (seg-rel 4000) shows the panel ASSEMBLED with 7 strikes already — the build expands the entrance: its grid phase (0–1200) draws panel+numerals with 0 strikes, so the build reaches "grid complete" at 1200 where the census has it at seg-rel 4000; every later anchor is then offset by the build's own phase durations, and the mapping below binds build states to census STATES (not to raw seg-rel arithmetic). (c) Census CP14000 (seg-rel 14000, transition out) has no build counterpart (deferral 3); the build's final hold stands in its place.
**State mapping (build instant → census state it must equal):** build 4400 (labels end) ≡ CP6000 state (strikes 20 · ringEarly ⊗ · ringLate plain · drops 2 · labelA struck · labelB present unstruck · tasks absent) · build 5400 (hold1 end) ≡ CP7000 state (identical — the hold) · build 6400 (tasks end) ≡ CP8000 state (tasks 3 rows · strikes 26 · calendar shifted) · build 8400 (sweep3 end) ≡ CP10000 state (tasks 5 rows · strikes 32) · build 10400 (final end) ≡ CP12000 state (strikes 35 — all cells marked · ringLate ⊗ · labelB struck · arc 0) · build 11400 (hold mid) ≡ CP12000 state (full-state equality, crack deferred).
**Comparison anchor table (jev-plan-exit charge 1 — the SAME map drives comparison.html and its Node check; build instants are CONFIG-derived phase ends, evaluated at runtime):**

| Source | Seg-rel | Cut-rel (cut @12.5 s) | Build instant (CONFIG expr) | Expected build state / departure |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 16.5 s partial entrance | 3500 | 4.0 s | grid phase interior (0–gridDurMs) | DEPARTURE: source already shows first-row strikes at 16.5 s; the build's grid phase is the allocated clean assembly (departure b) — the map's head shoulder covers 13–17 s |
| 17.0 s (CP4000) | 4000 | 4.5 s | gridDurMs = 1200 | Grid assembled; source has 7 strikes + day-16 plain ring + drop 1 + label A — the build at 1200 carries ringEarly formed + drop 1 + label A (set) but 0 strikes (departure b: strikes re-based into sweep 1) |
| 19.0 s (CP6000) | 6000 | 6.5 s | labelsStart + labelsDurMs = 4400 | P5 full predicate (CP6000 state) |
